<header class="main-header">
  <div class="series-title">Likutay Halachos &middot; Choshen Mishpat</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Da&rsquo;yonim 3 &mdash; Part 3</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Laws of Judges &mdash; 3 &middot; Osiyos 16&ndash;22</div>
</header>

<div class="continuation-note">
  Continued from Part 2 (Osiyos 9&ndash;15). Based on the teaching <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;T&rsquo;homos y&rsquo;chasyumu&rdquo;</span> in Likutay [Moharan] I, Siman 9.
</div>

<!-- ====== OS 16 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 16</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;testimony in Yaakov&rdquo;</span> [and] <span class="scripture">&ldquo;in Yehosayf&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 81:6)</span> &mdash; for they are the aspect of <span class="aramaic">train sahadai k&rsquo;shot</span> <span class="key-term-def">[two witnesses of truth]</span>, for Yaakov and Yosayf <span class="aramaic">k&rsquo;chada chashivai</span> <span class="key-term-def">[are reckoned as one]</span>, and they are the aspect of the two testimonies that each and every one of Yisroel possesses each day, through which they testify to His unity, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> &mdash; which are the aspects of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillin</span> and <span class="key-term">bris</span> <span class="key-term-def">[covenant]</span>. And on <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>: <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> and <span class="key-term">bris</span>, as is brought.
</p>

<p>
For Yaakov is the aspect of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillin</span>, which are called <span class="key-term">pe&rsquo;air</span> <span class="key-term-def">[splendor]</span>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic">shufraih d&rsquo;Yaakov</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the beauty of Yaakov]</span>. And likewise, Yaakov is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, for Yaakov kept the <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said regarding the verse <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And he encamped before the city&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 33:18)</span> &mdash; that he established <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;chumin</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Shabbos boundaries]</span> etc. And therefore our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Whoever keeps the Shabbos, they give him the inheritance of Yaakov&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Shabbos 118b)</span>, which is an <span class="scripture">&ldquo;inheritance without boundaries&rdquo;</span>. It emerges that Yaakov is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> and <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillin</span>.
</p>

<p>
And Yosayf is the aspect of <span class="key-term">bris</span> [covenant], as is known, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a Tzadik, the foundation of the world&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 10:25)</span>. And this is the aspect of the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> [intercalation], for Yosayf is the aspect of the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span>. For there are <span class="scripture">&ldquo;twelve tribes of Yah, a testimony for Yisroel, to give thanks to the Name of Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 122:4)</span> &mdash; which are the aspect of the twelve formulations of prayer etc., which is the aspect of the twelve windows through which the prayer ascends through the twelve gates etc., as above. And corresponding to this are the twelve lunar months &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span>, the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;lesser luminary,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of the contraction of the truth etc., as above.
</p>

<p>
And the intercalary month that they add &mdash; and then the year has thirteen months &mdash; this is the aspect of Yosayf, whose tribe was divided into two, and an additional tribe was added through him, corresponding to the intercalary month. For the essential <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> is in order to equalize the lunar year with the solar year &mdash; which is the aspect of the joining of the sun and the moon, so that the light of the moon should be like the light of the sun, and both should become one, as above. And this is accomplished through Yosayf, who is the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span>, who joins both of them &mdash; the sun and the moon, which are the two aforementioned aspects of truth &mdash; that is, he joins the twelve tribes of Yah, which are the twelve formulations of prayer etc., the twelve months, and he joins them to Yaakov, who is the very essence of truth, the aspect of the sun, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore Yaakov gave to Yosayf <span class="precise">specifically</span> <span class="scripture">&ldquo;one portion above your brothers&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 48:22)</span> &mdash; which is the birthright, that his tribe should be divided into two. For this is the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span>, as above. And as this verse is brought in the aforementioned teaching regarding prayer; see there. For the essential <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> and all its rectification is through <span class="key-term">emes</span>, and the <span class="key-term">emes</span> is the aspect of Yaakov. And it is impossible to receive the truth of Yaakov &mdash; which is the aspect of the very essence of truth &mdash; except through Yosayf, who is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a Tzadik, the foundation of the world,&rdquo;</span> who receives the truth from Yaakov and illuminates it among the generality of Yisroel, in the secret of <span class="key-term">s&rsquo;michas g&rsquo;ulah lis&rsquo;fillah</span> [juxtaposing redemption to prayer]. For <span class="key-term">g&rsquo;ulah</span> [redemption] is in <span class="key-term">Y&rsquo;sod</span> [Foundation], as is brought, which is Yosayf, who is <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a Tzadik, the foundation of the world,&rdquo;</span> who is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> of the generation, to whom one must connect all the prayers, and he elevates and clarifies all the prayers of Yisroel through the light of truth that illuminates within them.
</p>

<p>
And he joins the twelve tribes to Yaakov, for they are all included in Yosayf, as well, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And behold, the sun and the moon and eleven stars were bowing to me&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Genesis 37:9)</span> &mdash; for in him, in Yosayf, everything is included: sun and moon and twelve tribes. And therefore he joins them together and includes them together &mdash; and this is the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span>, through which the sun and the moon are joined and included together, as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Key parallel:</strong> Yaakov = sun = <em>emes</em> = <em>Shabbos</em> = <em>t&rsquo;fillin</em>. Yosayf = <em>bris</em> = <em>Y&rsquo;sod</em> = the <em>tzadik</em> who channels essential truth to the 12 tribes/12 prayers/12 months. Yosayf&rsquo;s tribe dividing into two = the 13th month of the leap year = the secret of <em>ibbur</em> (intercalation) that equalizes sun and moon. Yosayf&rsquo;s dream (sun, moon, and 11 stars bowing) = everything included in him, enabling the unification.
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 17 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 17</div>

<p>
And therefore a <span class="key-term">woman is disqualified from testifying</span>. For the essential testimony is to clarify and establish the truth that has fallen and been cast to the ground, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;and it cast truth to the ground&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Daniel 8:12)</span>, as above. And therefore the essential thing is to clarify and elevate the truth that is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon] &mdash; and this is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">woman</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, as is known. And therefore the woman cannot testify, for <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;a prisoner cannot free himself from prison&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Berachos 5b)</span>. And since this truth has been blemished &mdash; which is the aspect of the diminution of the moon, for the essential blemish reaches the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a woman who fears Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 31:30)</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> &mdash; therefore certainly the woman cannot raise up and clarify the truth, for she could also stumble in falsehood, since this truth has been blemished now through the falsehood of the litigants, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore two men are needed &mdash; adults of at least thirteen years &mdash; to testify. And they are the aspect of Yaakov and Yosayf, who are the aspect of the two witnesses, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;testimony in Yaakov,&rdquo;</span> <span class="scripture">&ldquo;testimony in Yehosayf,&rdquo;</span> as above &mdash; who join and unify the sun and the moon, the two aforementioned aspects of truth, which are the aspects of the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;great luminary&rdquo;</span> and the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;lesser luminary.&rdquo;</span> For this is the aspect of the greater witness and his fellow who is smaller than him, as it is written in the <span class="key-term">Mishnah</span>: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;They bring in the greater one first,&rdquo;</span> as above. And then the sun and the moon are included together &mdash; the two aforementioned aspects of truth &mdash; and become one, for in truth it is all one. And then the falsehood is repelled and the truth ascends, as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 18 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 18</div>

<p>
And therefore <span class="key-term">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the sanctification of the new month]</span> and the <span class="key-term">ibbur shonim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[intercalation of years]</span> was through the <span class="key-term">bais din</span> and witnesses, for they establish the truth and join the sun and the moon, as above &mdash; and this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Kiddush HaChodesh</span> and the <span class="key-term">intercalation of years</span>, as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 19 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 19</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Purim Gadol</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the &ldquo;Great&rdquo; Purim]</span> and <span class="key-term">Purim Katan</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the &ldquo;Small&rdquo; Purim]</span> that are observed in a leap year. For one only intercalates Adar, because Adar is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth], as Rabbainu, <em>zichrono livrachah</em>, wrote: that <strong>A-Da-R</strong> is an acronym of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<strong>R</strong>osh <strong>D</strong>&rsquo;varcha <strong>E</strong>mes&rdquo;</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;The beginning of Your word is truth&rdquo;]</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 119:160)</span>. And therefore the essential miracle of Purim occurred in Adar, in which the year is intercalated.
</p>

<p>
For the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span> is the aspect of the obliteration of the memory of Amalek. For the intercalation of the year &mdash; which is the joining of the sun and the moon, the two aforementioned aspects of truth, and everything becomes one, for <span class="key-term">emes</span> is one, as above &mdash; this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Shem Sholam</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Full Name]</span>, which is the Name <span class="key-term">Hashem Elokim</span> becoming one, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is One and His Name is One,&rdquo;</span> which is the essential aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Hashem <em>Elokim</em> is truth,&rdquo;</span> as above. And this is the aspect of the obliteration of Haman-Amalek, for the Holy One, Blessed is He, swore that the <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Name is not complete and the Throne is not complete until the memory of Amalek is obliterated&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Rashi, Exodus 17:16)</span>.
</p>

<p>
For Amalek is the contamination of the Serpent, the aspect of <span class="key-term">sheker</span> [falsehood], for Amalek denied the essential [faith], and he is the blemish of <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> [prayer], and he is the essential darkness and confusion that intensify at the time of prayer. And his essential power is over the weak of Yisroel, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And he struck the stragglers among you, all the feeble ones at your rear, and you were weary and exhausted etc.&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 25:18)</span> &mdash; that is, over those whose prayer is weak, whose truth is in the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>. There he seeks to overpower, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, to turn the truth to falsehood, surrounding them with falsehoods that are the alien thoughts and confusions, not allowing them to pray.
</p>

<p>
And therefore the essential downfall of Haman-Amalek is through <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;fillah</span> [prayer]; that is, when one strengthens and arouses the truth upon himself in whatever capacity, as above &mdash; and then one merits to see the openings to exit from the darkness [and] from the <span class="key-term">k&rsquo;lipas</span> [husk of] Amalek, and one merits to go from darkness to light, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The Jews had light&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Esther 8:16)</span> &mdash; which was stated regarding the downfall of Haman-Amalek.
</p>

<p>
However, it is impossible to merit that one&rsquo;s small measure of truth should illuminate except through meriting to draw close to <span class="key-term">tzadikay emes</span> <span class="key-term-def">[tzadikim of truth]</span>, who are the aspect of the very essence of truth that illuminates in each and every point of truth that exists in each and every one of Yisroel, even in the most lowly of the lowly and the worst of the worst.
</p>

<p>
And this is what is written regarding the war with Amalek: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Moshe said to Yehoshua: Go out and fight against Amalek&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 17:9)</span>. For the essential downfall of Amalek is through Yehoshua <span class="precise">specifically</span>, who is suited for this, as is found in the holy Zohar. For Yehoshua is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> [moon], in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;The face of Moshe was like the face of the sun; the face of Yehoshua was like the face of the moon&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Bava Basra 75a)</span>. For the essential hold of Amalek is from the diminution of the moon, which is the blemish of the truth that is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, as above. And therefore his downfall is through Yehoshua, who is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> &mdash; that is, the aspect of the rectification of the blemish of the moon, through which Amalek falls: when the truth of the truth that each and every one of Yisroel possesses is clarified, which is the aspect of the filling of the blemish of the moon, as above.
</p>

<p>
But it is impossible for Yehoshua to fight the war of Amalek &mdash; to illuminate the illumination of truth &mdash; except through Moshe, his master, who is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chamah</span> [sun], as above, the aspect of the very essence of truth. And this is what the verse states regarding the war with Amalek: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And his hands were <em>emunah</em> [faith/steadfast] until the coming of the sun&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 17:12)</span>. And the Targum renders: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;spread out in prayer.&rdquo;</span> For Moshe is the aspect of the very essence of truth, the aspect of the sun illuminating the prayer, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;<em>emunah</em> until the coming of the sun&rdquo;</span> &mdash; until he brought and drew the light of the sun, the light of the very essence of truth, into the prayer. For this is the aspect of the filling of the blemish of the moon &mdash; and this rectification Yehoshua receives from Moshe, and through this he fights the war of Amalek and illuminates the truth in each and every one of Yisroel, so that each one merits to see the openings within the great darkness that surrounds at the time of prayer, and they go from darkness to light and pray well. For this is the aspect of the downfall of Amalek, who is the darkness, the aspect of falsehood etc., as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore Moshe and Yehoshua caused the sun to stand still &mdash; in the war with Amalek and in the war against the thirty-one kings &mdash; to show that they fill the blemish of the moon and draw the light of the sun to the light of the moon, until they were able to draw the light of the sun even at night, for everything is one &mdash; sun and moon &mdash; and they are included together, as above.
</p>

<p>
It emerges that the essential downfall of Haman is through the filling of the blemish of the moon, which is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;and the light of the moon shall be like the light of the sun&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 30:26)</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of the filling of the Name, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Full Name</span>, which is the aspect of the secret of <span class="key-term">ibbur</span>, as above. And therefore the essential miracle of Purim occurred in Adar, in which the year is intercalated, as above. And this is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;words of peace and truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Esther 9:30)</span>, that Mordechai and Esther merited to draw the light of truth, which is the essential light, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the Jews had light,&rdquo;</span> as above &mdash; and this is the essential downfall of Haman-Amalek, as above.
</p>

<div class="word-note">
<strong>Key teaching:</strong> Amalek = the darkness/falsehood that attacks prayer, especially in the weak. His downfall comes specifically through Yehoshua (the moon &mdash; the very level Amalek attacks) empowered by Moshe (the sun = essential truth). <em>Purim</em> occurred in <em>Adar</em> because Adar = <em>emes</em> (acronym of &ldquo;Rosh D&rsquo;varcha Emes&rdquo;), and the leap-year intercalation of Adar = the secret of <em>ibbur</em> = joining sun and moon = completing the Full Name = obliterating Amalek.
</div>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 20 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 20</div>

<p>
And therefore the essential miracle was through Esther, who is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a woman who fears Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 31:30)</span>, the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, as above. For Haman wished then specifically to overpower Yisroel, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, at the time when Esther was taken to the house of the king &mdash; for this was the essential blemish of the truth, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, the aspect of the diminution of the moon. For he reasoned that the aspect of Esther &mdash; the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> etc., the aspect of the second type of truth mentioned above &mdash; had been drawn into the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span>, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, since she was taken to the bed of the uncircumcised one. And then the essential sustenance of the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> &mdash; whose sustenance comes from there, from the aspect of the descent of the second type of truth mentioned above among the <span class="key-term">k&rsquo;lipos</span>, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em> &mdash; and therefore he wished then to overpower Yisroel, for his essential power comes from this blemish of the truth that is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span> etc., as above.
</p>

<p>
And his essential power was through the blemish of the <span class="key-term">bris</span> [covenant] that existed then, for they had stumbled with foreign women, who are from <span class="aramaic">sitra d&rsquo;shikra</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the side of falsehood]</span>. For guarding the <span class="key-term">bris</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;all of them are seed of truth.&rdquo;</span> Which is the aspect of the rectification of prayer, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">zivug dik&rsquo;dusha</span> <span class="key-term-def">[holy union]</span>, the aspect of the joining of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, sun and moon, as above and as explained in the aforementioned teaching &mdash; which is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;their union is as difficult as the splitting of the Sea of Reeds&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Sotah 2a)</span> etc. But union that is not in holiness is the aspect of the blemish of truth, and <em>kal va&rsquo;chomer</em> [all the more so] the blemish of <span class="key-term">nidah</span>, <span class="key-term">shifchah</span>, <span class="key-term">goyah</span>, <span class="key-term">zonah</span>, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em> &mdash; this is the essential aspect of falsehood, as is found in the holy Zohar: <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Whoever <em>falsifies</em> the holy covenant.&rdquo;</span> <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;<em>Falsifies</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="precise">specifically</span>, for the nations are from the aspect of falsehood, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Whose mouth speaks vanity, and their right hand is a right hand of falsehood&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 144:8)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And because of this &mdash; that they blemished with foreign women &mdash; through this they caused the blemish to reach the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a woman who fears Hashem,&rdquo;</span> which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>. And through this Esther was taken to the house of the king, and Haman reasoned that through this he would overpower Yisroel, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, for a separation had been made, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, between <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, between the sun and the moon, through the blemish of the <span class="key-term">bris</span>, from which is the essential hold of Haman-Amalek, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, as above. And therefore there was indeed then a very, very great distress.
</p>

<p>
But Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> was good to us and performed for us miracles and great and awesome wonders in every generation, and He sent then Mordechai and Esther, who are the aspects of the sun and the moon, <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>. And not only was Esther not blemished, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, through being taken to the house of the king; on the contrary, through this she brought forth light from within the darkness. For Achashveirosh did not touch her at all, as is found in the holy Zohar.
</p>

<p>
And the essential means of her deliverance was through <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth], as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: when Esther entered the house of Achashveirosh, which was full of idols, she was crying out: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;My G-d, my G-d, why have You forsaken me?!&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 22:2)</span>. For this is the essential rectification &mdash; to exit from the darkness, as above &mdash; that is, when the great darkness intensifies upon a proper person who wishes to draw near to Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, and especially at the time of prayer, and the darkness surrounds him from every side and from every direction &mdash; this is the aspect of the entry of Esther, who is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of the holy point that is hidden within each and every one of Yisroel, that enters, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, into the house of the wicked Achashveirosh, into a house full of idols and filth &mdash; which is the aspect of the extreme intensification of the darkness, and he knows no way or counsel or strategy to be saved from them.
</p>

<p>
And then the essential counsel is only <span class="key-term">emes</span>: that he should speak the utterance in truth and cry out to Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> in truth &mdash; which is the aspect of what Esther cried out when she entered the house full of idols, crying out: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;My G-d, my G-d, why have You forsaken me?!&rdquo;</span> And through this the light of truth illuminated for her, drawn upon her from the aspect of Mordechai, who is the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> of the generation, the aspect of the very essence of truth. And through this she was saved from the bed of the uncircumcised one, for he did not touch her, <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;because a brother guarded her, which is the point of the letter <em>dalet</em> of <em>Echad</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Tikkunim)</span> &mdash; that is, the very essence of truth, which is the unity of Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, which is the very essence of truth, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is my light,&rdquo;</span> which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">K&rsquo;rias Sh&rsquo;ma</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Hashem is One,&rdquo;</span> as above. This guarded Esther, and this guards each and every one of Yisroel when he cries out to Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> in truth &mdash; even if he has fallen to whatever place he has fallen, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, even if the darkness surrounds him from all sides. Nevertheless, when he believes in Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> in truth, in simplicity, believing in Hashem <span class="key-term">Echad</span> [Who is One], and cries out to Him in truth &mdash; <span class="scripture">&ldquo;My G-d, my G-d, why have You forsaken me?!&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and supplicates Him in truth, then the truth illuminates for him, and he sees the openings, and he goes from darkness to light, as above.
</p>

<p>
And then, not only can the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> and the darkness not prevent him and confuse his prayer, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>, he even merits to make an opening also for others &mdash; to bring others out from the darkness and to bring them back in <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;shuvah</span> [repentance], as is explained there in Siman 112 regarding the verse <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And the opening of the <em>taivah</em> you shall place at its side&rdquo;</span>; see there. For this is the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And many of the peoples of the land became Jews&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Esther 8:17)</span> &mdash; that Esther merited through her truth, through which she was saved from Achashveirosh and clarified the truth from the falsehood, and she was not distanced from Mordechai, <em>chas v&rsquo;sholom</em>. And on the contrary, the blemish of the moon was filled through them &mdash; through Mordechai and Esther &mdash; through her clarifying the truth from the falsehood, to the point that many converted, as above. For this is the aspect of the joining of the two aforementioned aspects of truth &mdash; the aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, Mordechai and Esther &mdash; which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Full Name</span>, as above.
</p>

<p>
And therefore the miracle occurred in Adar, in which the year is intercalated, as above. For this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Purim Gadol</span> and <span class="key-term">Purim Katan</span>, the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the great luminary&rdquo;</span> and <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the lesser luminary&rdquo;</span> &mdash; which are the sun and the moon, Mordechai and Esther &mdash; who were included together, and the blemish of the moon was filled, and the truth was revealed, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;words of peace and truth,&rdquo;</span> as above. And therefore they accepted the Torah anew then, as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;They established and they accepted&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Esther 9:27)</span> &mdash; for the Torah is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above, and this is the essential downfall of Haman &mdash; through truth, as above. And this is what our Sages, of blessed memory, said: that the <span class="key-term">Megillah</span> requires <span class="key-term">sirtut</span> <span class="key-term-def">[scored lines]</span> <span class="scripture">&ldquo;like the truth of the Torah&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Megillah 16b)</span> &mdash; for the <span class="key-term">Megillah</span> is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the truth of the Torah,&rdquo;</span> the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;a Torah of truth&rdquo;</span> &mdash; for this is the essential downfall of Haman-Amalek mentioned above, who is the darkness surrounding at the time of prayer, that falls and is nullified through the truth, which is the essential light to see the openings, as above, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the Jews had light,&rdquo;</span> as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 21 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 21</div>

<p>
And therefore on Purim one must give abundantly in <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> [charity], in the aspect of <span class="key-term">matanos la&rsquo;evyonim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[gifts to the poor]</span>. For through the <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> that the giver gives to the poor recipient, through this one fills the blemish of the moon, as is known. For the recipient is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of <span class="aramaic">ispaklaryah d&rsquo;lo nahara mi&rsquo;garmah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a lens that does not shine of its own]</span>, that has nothing of its own. And the one who bestows the <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> is the aspect of the sun, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And the sun of <em>tzedakah</em> shall rise upon you who fear My Name&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Malachi 3:20)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And therefore through <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> one merits truth, as Rabbainu, <em>zichrono livrachah</em>, wrote in Seifer Ha&rsquo;Alef-Beis (<em>Emes</em>, Siman 15), and as it is written: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And one who sows <em>tzedakah</em> [reaps] a reward of truth&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Proverbs 11:18)</span>. For this is the essential light of truth: when the sun and the moon are joined together, as above &mdash; and this is the essential aspect of Purim, as above. And therefore one must give abundantly in <span class="key-term">tzedakah</span> on Purim, as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 22 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 22</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, which is the aspect of testimony to His unity, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said. And therefore the commandment <span class="scripture">&ldquo;You shall not bear [false] witness&rdquo;</span> corresponds to <span class="scripture">&ldquo;Remember the day of Shabbos&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(see Mechilta)</span>, for <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> is the aspect of testimony, as is brought in the words of our Sages, of blessed memory.
</p>

<p>
And therefore they arrange the <span class="key-term">Lechem HaPonim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Showbread]</span> on <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> &mdash; which are twelve loaves, which are the aspect of the twelve tribes etc., as above &mdash; and all of them are included in the two rows, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">lechem mishneh</span> <span class="key-term-def">[double bread]</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Mishneh Torah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the repetition of the Torah]</span> &mdash; the Written Torah and the Oral Torah &mdash; which is the aspect of the two witnesses who clarify the truth, as above.
</p>

<p>
For <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> is the very essence of truth, the aspect of the sun, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the sun on Shabbos is <em>tzedakah</em>&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Ta&rsquo;anis 8b)</span>. For <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> is <span class="aramaic">k&rsquo;vi&rsquo;ah v&rsquo;kayama</span> <span class="key-term-def">[fixed and enduring]</span>, whereas <span class="key-term">Yom Tov</span> &mdash; <span class="aramaic">&ldquo;Yisroel are the ones who sanctify them&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Beitzah 17a)</span>. That is, <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> is the very essence of truth, the aspect of the light of Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, which is the truth that is fixed and enduring and never changes, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;And Your word is truth and endures forever&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 119:160)</span>. But the <span class="key-term">Yomim Tovim</span> [festivals] are in the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, in the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;He made the moon for the appointed times&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 104:19)</span> &mdash; which depends upon Yisroel, who sanctify the months and intercalate the years. And therefore we say <span class="scripture">&ldquo;[Who] sanctifies Yisroel and the appointed times&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(see Berachos 49a)</span>, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said. That is, the sanctity of <span class="key-term">Yom Tov</span> is the aspect of going from exile [to freedom], for all the festivals are a remembrance of the Exodus from Egypt, which encompasses all the exiles, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said &mdash; that is, when one goes from darkness to light through the light of truth, and one can pray, as above. And therefore there are <span class="key-term">Sholosh Regolim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Three Pilgrimage Festivals]</span> corresponding to the three daily prayers, whose rectification is through truth.
</p>

<p>
And therefore the essential rectification of the festivals is through the <span class="key-term">bais din</span>, who are the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, who intercalate the years and establish the months. And this truth, which is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">l&rsquo;vanah</span>, the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, is according to the sanctity of Yisroel, upon whom the sanctity of the festivals depends, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;These are the appointed times of Hashem that you shall call them in their appointed time&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 23:4)</span>, as our Sages, of blessed memory, said <span class="source">(Rosh Hashanah 24a)</span>.
</p>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the sun knows its setting&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 104:19)</span>, but the moon does not know its setting, for sometimes it comes in a long [cycle] and sometimes it comes in a short [cycle]. For the sun, which is the very essence of truth, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> that is fixed and enduring &mdash; this truth never changes, and falsehood has no hold in it whatsoever. For this is the aspect of the truth of the <span class="key-term">tzadik</span> of truth, which is the truth that endures forever, and there is no change in it whatsoever, and it is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the sun knows its setting.&rdquo;</span> But <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the moon does not know its setting&rdquo;</span> &mdash; that is, this truth that is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span>, the aspect of the moon. And this truth is the aspect of Esther, which is hidden and concealed for each and every person according to his level and degree, and it is impossible to know the setting and the way of this truth, for sometimes it comes in a long [form] and sometimes in a short [form]. This is the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;whether one does much or one does little, as long as he directs his heart toward Heaven&rdquo;</span> <span class="source">(Berachos 5b)</span>.
</p>

<p>
For one who desires truth and walks in the way of truth &mdash; it is impossible to know his way, for sometimes it comes at length and sometimes briefly; sometimes he lengthens his prayer, sometimes he shortens it, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">&ldquo;whether one does much or one does little, as long as he directs his heart toward Heaven.&rdquo;</span> For this is the aspect of truth: the essential thing is that he should direct his heart toward Heaven in truth. And he needs only to receive the light of truth each time from the <span class="key-term">tzadikay emes</span> [tzadikim of truth], who are the very essence of truth, and according to the truth that he receives from them, according to the time and the moment, according to what they need to illuminate within him, according to his level &mdash; so he must go and conduct himself.
</p>

<p>
But <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> is fixed and enduring &mdash; it is the very essence of truth, as above. For from <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> all the <span class="key-term">Sholosh Regolim</span> receive, for they too are called &ldquo;<span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>,&rdquo; as we say: <span class="scripture">&ldquo;the beginning of the holy convocations etc.&rdquo;</span> For in truth, everything is one &mdash; <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> and <span class="key-term">Yom Tov</span>, sun and moon etc., as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== OS 23 ====== -->
<div class="os-header">Os 23</div>

<p>
And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Tosefes Shabbos</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the addition to Shabbos]</span>, that one adds from the weekday onto the holy [day] &mdash; at its entry and its departure &mdash; through which one draws the sanctity of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays. For also during the weekdays we need to sanctify ourselves through Torah and <span class="key-term">mitzvos</span>, which are the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>. But the truth of the weekdays is the aspect of a <span class="key-term">window</span> etc., as above, which needs to receive the light of the very essence of truth from <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>. And therefore one must add from the weekday onto the holy [day], in order to draw the light of truth from <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> into the weekdays, as above.
</p>

<p>
For on <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> they join together <span class="key-term">Zachor</span> and <span class="key-term">Shamor</span> <span class="key-term-def">[&ldquo;Remember&rdquo; and &ldquo;Guard&rdquo;]</span>, which are the aspects of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, sun and moon, as is known. And therefore the essential <span class="key-term">zivug</span> <span class="key-term-def">[marital union]</span> of <span class="key-term">talmidai chachomim</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Torah scholars]</span> is from <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> to <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span> <span class="source">(Kesubos 62b)</span>, for the essential sanctity of the <span class="key-term">zivug</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as above &mdash; the aspect of the joining of <span class="key-term">emes</span> and <span class="key-term">emunah</span> etc., as above.
</p>

<div class="section-divider">&bull; &bull; &bull;</div>

<!-- ====== TRANSLATOR SUMMARY ====== -->
<div class="translator-summary">
<h3>Translator&rsquo;s Summary &mdash; Osiyos 16&ndash;23</h3>

<p>
These eight sections extend the sun/moon framework into testimony, the calendar, Purim, and Shabbos. <strong>Os 16</strong> identifies Yaakov and Yosayf as the two archetypal witnesses: Yaakov = sun = Shabbos = t&rsquo;fillin = essential truth; Yosayf = bris = Y&rsquo;sod = the tzadik who channels truth to the 12 tribes = the 13th month of the leap year (his tribe dividing into two). <strong>Os 17</strong> explains why a woman cannot testify: she corresponds to the moon/Malchus/window &mdash; the very aspect that has been blemished &mdash; and &ldquo;a prisoner cannot free himself.&rdquo; <strong>Os 18</strong> is a brief summation: Kiddush HaChodesh and intercalation depend on bais din and witnesses because they embody truth and join sun and moon.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Os 19</strong> is a major section on Purim: Adar = emes (acronym of &ldquo;Rosh D&rsquo;varcha Emes&rdquo;); Amalek = falsehood/darkness attacking prayer, especially in the weak; his downfall through Yehoshua (moon) empowered by Moshe (sun); the intercalation of Adar = the Full Name = obliterating Amalek. <strong>Os 20</strong> applies this to the Purim narrative in detail: Esther (moon/Malchus) taken to the house of Achashveirosh = the blemished truth seemingly captured by the Sitra Achara. But she cried out &ldquo;My G-d, my G-d, why have You forsaken me?!&rdquo; in truth, and the essential truth (Mordechai = sun) illuminated within her and protected her. This paradigm applies to every Jew surrounded by darkness: cry out in truth, even from the lowest place, and the truth will illuminate openings to exit. <strong>Os 21</strong> connects Purim charity (matanos la&rsquo;evyonim) to filling the moon&rsquo;s blemish: the giver = sun, the poor recipient = window/moon. <strong>Os 22</strong> maps Shabbos as essential fixed truth (sun) versus Yom Tov as variable truth (moon) that depends on Yisroel&rsquo;s sanctification; &ldquo;the sun knows its setting&rdquo; but &ldquo;the moon does not know its setting&rdquo; = each person&rsquo;s truth varies, &ldquo;whether one does much or one does little, as long as he directs his heart toward Heaven.&rdquo; <strong>Os 23</strong> explains Tosefes Shabbos (adding from weekday to Shabbos) as drawing the essential truth of Shabbos into the weekdays.
</p>

<p class="translator-note">
&mdash; Translator&rsquo;s summary. Not part of the original text.
</p>
</div>

